# creature-evolution v1 (LOCKED GATE 3) — vars: {name}, {prior_stage_name}, {design_brief}, {palette_rows}
# model: flux_2 pro 1k, aspect 1:1, medias: [prior stage front job as reference]
# output feeds postprocess.py --kind battle
Pixel art game creature battle sprite, front three-quarter view facing slightly
left, full body. Creature: {name}, the EVOLVED FORM of the creature in the
reference image ({prior_stage_name}). Keep clear family resemblance: same
species' face markings, same color identity, recognizably the same animal grown
into: {design_brief}. Bigger, more imposing silhouette than the reference —
silhouette growth, not just scale. Colors strictly from: {palette_rows}.
GBA Pokemon FireRed era style, flat cel shading, no gradients, crisp 1px very
dark outline, maximum 15 colors, strong silhouette. Plain solid white
background, centered, no text, no watermark.
